#+TITLE: AutoCAD heap corruption at exit after SCHME historical tests
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: native-cad-validation

* Reproduction evidence
SCHME MR339 HEAD04bc0747 pipeline92968 job571171: 23/23, RESTORED,
close-owned.result0, installation/profile restored. Independent read-only Win32
observer retained PID12788/creation639294764853052918 before Quit and observed
native exit3221226356 (C0000374). No process was killed.
The disposable profile log path existed and was isolated to job571171.
ALFE sourcea6636dca (private2.3.96) and shared harness5a502b6 are recorded.

* Scope
The restoration-log defect is independently fixed. The heap failure's originating
writer/component is not identified; do not attribute it to a DLL or to ALFE from
an exit code alone. Relate to the independently documented EPURE clean-profile
exit issue on the newer ALFE development line, but retain the distinct identity.
Native exit zero remains mandatory for qualification. No whitelist or GEP
assertion tolerance may accept this failure.

* Follow-up: 2026-11-05, strict native gate
SCHME job 571365, ALFE 2.3.97, passed 23 assertions and reached RESTORED.
Both disposable profile and installation restoration manifests are true.
The retained native handle reported 47806 (0xBABE), PID 8320, creation
FILETIME 134383562765928623. This differs from the earlier 0xC0000374;
no common cause or documented successful-exit contract is established.
The job correctly failed. No nonzero native exit is accepted.
A separate 2.3.98 experiment waits for bounded COM quiescence after the
protocol returns and before closing any document. Its absence was a
lifecycle gap; whether it explains either exit code remains unproven.
BricsCAD job 571366 reached RESTORED and 23/23 but native close was refused
because 2.3.97 read AutoCAD-only com-flags.txt. The shared bridge in 2.3.98
writes its own ownership flags for both engines. This is an ALFE regression,
not a BricsCAD native exit result, and is unrelated to AutoCAD 0xBABE.

* 2026-11-06 qualification with calibrated normal exit
Two stock AutoCAD R24.1.203.0.0 safe-mode launches without EPURE (job572688,
ordinary and Automation) exited47806/BABE after successful COM Quit, without
force. ALFE99 recognizes only this acad.exe SHA-256 for BABE, not arbitrary
binaries. Job572696 then passed23/23, reachedRESTORED and restored its profile
and installation, but the retained kernel handle reportedC0000005, PID376,
FILETIME134384301259637093. It correctly failed, without a normality marker.
The contemporaneous Application event query returned no matching events; this
does not negate the kernel exit observation. No native module is attributed.
ALFE100 makes Close/release/quiescent/Quit separate steps, matching the successful
stock diagnostic; its causal effect on this native fault remains to be tested.
